.TH C-EXPENSE 1 "2026-05-13" "c-expense 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
c-expense \- simple command-line expense tracker
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B c-expense
.RI [COMMAND]
.RI [OPTIONS]
.br
.B c-expense add
.RB [ \-t " | " \-\-title " " \fITITLE\fR]
.RB [ \-a " | " \-\-amount " " \fIAMOUNT\fR]
.RB [ \-c " | " \-\-category " " \fICATEGORY\fR]
.RB [ \-d " | " \-\-date " " \fIDATE\fR]
.br
.B c-expense delete
.RB \-i " | " \-\-id " " \fIID\fR
.br
.B c-expense list
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B c-expense
is a minimal expense tracker backed by SQLite. Expenses are stored locally and can be added, listed, and deleted from the command line.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add
Add a new expense.
.TP
.B delete
Delete an expense by ID.
.TP
.B list
List all expenses.
.SH OPTIONS
For the
.B add
command:
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-title " " \fITITLE\fR
Title or description of the expense. Required.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-amount " " \fIAMOUNT\fR
Amount of the expense, e.g. \fI10\fR or \fI10.50\fR. Required.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-category " " \fICATEGORY\fR
Category of the expense, e.g. \fIfood\fR, \fItransport\fR, \fIrent\fR. Optional.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-date " " \fIDATE\fR
Date of the expense. Format \fIDD/MM\fR or \fIDD/MM/YYYY\fR, e.g. \fI10/09\fR. If year is omitted, current year is assumed. Optional.

For the
.B delete
command:
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-id " " \fIID\fR
ID of the expense to delete. The ID is shown in the output of \fBc-expense list\fR. Required.

The
.B list
command takes no options.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Delete expense with ID 10:
.B c-expense delete -i 10
.TP
Add lunch expense:
.B c-expense add --title lunch --amount 10 --category food --date 10/09
.TP
Same using short flags:
.B c-expense add -t lunch -a 10 -c food -d 10/09
.TP
List all expenses grouped by day of week:
.B c-expense list
.SH FILES
.TP
.I./expenses.db
Default SQLite database file (or path defined by DB_FILE at compile time).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failure (database error, missing arguments, or invalid input).
.SH AUTHOR
Written by JakeSiewJK64.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sqlite3 (1)
